## Report
Attempted dynamic reproduction first: host is x86_64 (uname -m). `cargo build -p checksum --features pure-rust --target aarch64-unknown-linux-gnu` failed due to cross-compiling ec-sys (libisal/pkg-config missing). Retried with `--no-default-features --features pure-rust`, but rustc reported the aarch64 target is not installed. valgrind and gdb are not available in the container, so crash/valgrind/debugger reproduction could not be performed here. Code review confirms the issue: in crc32.rs, the aarch64 backend is selected via `has_crc_pmull_aarch64()` (pure_rust_backend at crc32.rs:170-174), but that check only tests `crc` and `aes` (crc32.rs:203-206) and omits `pmull`. The aarch64 fast path uses `vmull_p64` under `#[target_feature(enable = "crc,neon,aes")]` (crc32.rs:493-499), which requires PMULL instructions. The same pattern exists in crc32c.rs (backend selection at 169-173, detection at 202-206, PMULL usage at 476-482). On hardware with AES+CRC but no PMULL, the runtime detection will incorrectly choose the PMULL path and execute `vmull_p64`, leading to an illegal-instruction crash.

